    {
      "id": "claim_b6a1aed9483d486ba0e1a0da7136ffbc",
      "statement": "Two independent close signals feed the lifecycle derivation owned by two different steps: bronSaysClosed and sluitingsdatumPassed come from the normaliser and yield closed, with seenOpen checked after the close signals so closed always outranks active; missedPolls is counted per complete listing run at the run boundary (reconcileMissedPolls) and yields stale, never closed. closed therefore always outranks stale: a date-closed record that also disappears stays closed, and a stale record whose source later publishes a closing date becomes closed through the normaliser path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/application/src/lifecycle/reconcile-missed-polls.ts#L153-L210",
