    {
      "id": "claim_f1b295b92ad04e53a269c228e40891d3",
      "statement": "The Boolean parser is a hand-written tokenizer plus recursive-descent parser. Keywords OR, AND, NOT are matched case-insensitively but only when not part of a larger term. Precedence is NOT (tightest), then AND (explicit and implicit — adjacent terms without an operator form an AND), then OR. Parentheses group; an unclosed parenthesis, unclosed phrase, empty query, missing operand, or unexpected token all produce a syntax_error with an offset.",
